      "source": [
        "# BCSE 1593 – Data Science and Visualization Lab\n",
        "## NumPy Practice Set\n",
        "\n",
        "### Case Study: Managing Data for a Smart Campus\n",
        "\n",
        "The university is planning a **Smart Campus Management System**. Different departments are collecting numerical information such as electricity consumption, student attendance, classroom occupancy, library visits and canteen sales.\n",
        "\n",
        "You are working as a junior data analyst. Before this information is used for reports and dashboards, you need to organize and analyse it using **NumPy**.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this practice set, you will work with small datasets similar to the type of data that a real campus system may generate.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Instructions\n",
        "\n",
        "- Complete the questions in the given order.\n",
        "- Write your own NumPy code in the empty cells.\n",
        "- Try to solve the questions using NumPy operations instead of Python loops.\n",
        "- Display the output wherever it helps you understand the result.\n",
        "- Use meaningful variable names.\n",
        "- Do not change the given data unless a question specifically asks you to create a new array.\n",
        "- If you get an error, first check the array's **shape, indexing and dimensions**.\n"
      ],
      "id": "NPlg1NJr-0VP"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "EgxM4O9a-0VR"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Dataset for the Practice\n",
        "\n",
        "The following data has been collected from three campus facilities:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Academic Block**\n",
        "- **Library**\n",
        "- **Hostel**\n",
        "\n",
        "For the monthly datasets, rows represent months and columns represent facilities.\n"
      ],
      "id": "EgxM4O9a-0VR"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "dZ1HPZWx-0VS",
        "outputId": "e277f7aa-4149-43db-a88a-3fbbdbc9f6f2"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Data loaded successfully.\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# Monthly electricity consumption in kWh\n",
        "# Columns: Academic Block, Library, Hostel\n",
        "monthly_energy = np.array([\n",
        "    [42000, 18500, 31000],\n",
        "    [43500, 19200, 31800],\n",
        "    [44800, 20100, 32500],\n",
        "    [46200, 21500, 33100],\n",
        "    [47800, 22100, 34000],\n",
        "    [49500, 23000, 35200],\n",
        "    [51000, 23800, 36000],\n",
        "    [52500, 24600, 37100],\n",
        "    [51800, 24100, 36500],\n",
        "    [50200, 23200, 35400],\n",
        "    [47500, 21800, 33900],\n",
        "    [45000, 20500, 32500]\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Monthly student visits\n",
        "# Columns: Academic Block, Library, Hostel\n",
        "monthly_visits = np.array([\n",
        "    [8200, 5400, 6100],\n",
        "    [8500, 5600, 6250],\n",
        "    [8700, 5750, 6400],\n",
        "    [9100, 5900, 6650],\n",
        "    [9500, 6200, 6900],\n",
        "    [9800, 6500, 7200],\n",
        "    [10200, 6800, 7500],\n",
        "    [10400, 7000, 7700],\n",
        "    [10100, 6750, 7450],\n",
        "    [9600, 6300, 7000],\n",
        "    [9000, 5900, 6650],\n",
        "    [8600, 5650, 6350]\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Classroom occupancy percentage for one week\n",
        "# Rows = days, Columns = five classrooms\n",
        "weekly_occupancy = np.array([\n",
        "    [72, 68, 81, 75, 63],\n",
        "    [78, 71, 85, 80, 66],\n",
        "    [82, 74, 88, 83, 69],\n",
        "    [76, 70, 84, 79, 64],\n",
        "    [90, 86, 92, 88, 73],\n",
        "    [58, 61, 55, 63, 49],\n",
        "    [42, 38, 45, 40, 35]\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Daily canteen sales for two weeks\n",
        "canteen_sales = np.array([\n",
        "    [18500, 17200, 19300, 20100, 21400],\n",
        "    [19200, 18100, 20500, 21800, 22500],\n",
        "    [17600, 16900, 18800, 19600, 20800],\n",
        "    [21000, 19800, 22100, 23000, 24200],\n",
        "    [22500, 21400, 23800, 24600, 25500],\n",
        "    [14200, 13600, 15100, 16000, 16800],\n",
        "    [12500, 11900, 13200, 14100, 14800],\n",
        "    [18900, 17800, 20100, 21000, 22000],\n",
        "    [19500, 18400, 20800, 21900, 22800],\n",
        "    [18100, 17300, 19200, 20200, 21100]\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Temperature readings from campus equipment\n",
        "equipment_temperature = np.array(\n",
        "    [24.5, 25.1, 23.8, 27.4, 29.2, 26.8, 31.5, 22.9, 28.1, 30.4]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "months = np.array([\n",
        "    \"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Apr\", \"May\", \"Jun\",\n",
        "    \"Jul\", \"Aug\", \"Sep\", \"Oct\", \"Nov\", \"Dec\"\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "facilities = np.array([\"Academic Block\", \"Library\", \"Hostel\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Data loaded successfully.\")\n"
      ],
      "id": "dZ1HPZWx-0VS"
    },
