      "source": [
        "# Part A – Creating and Understanding Arrays\n",
        "\n",
        "### Question 1 – A small campus record\n",
        "\n",
        "The security department records the number of students entering the campus at five different times:\n",
        "\n",
        "`[125, 180, 210, 165, 95]`\n",
        "\n",
        "Create a NumPy array called `entry_count`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Display:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. The array\n",
        "2. Its type\n",
        "3. Its shape\n",
        "4. Its data type\n"
      ],
      "id": "ONtAYOrR-0VT"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "et95BD9L-0VT",
        "outputId": "e8bed09f-7bcd-44ee-c9ba-fcc3ac456007"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[125 180 210 165  95]\n",
            "<class 'numpy.ndarray'>\n",
            "(5,)\n",
            "int64\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 1 here\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "student_array = [125,180,210,165,95]\n",
        "entry_count = np.array(student_array)\n",
        "print(entry_count)\n",
        "print(type(entry_count))\n",
        "print(entry_count.shape)\n",
        "print(entry_count.dtype)"
      ],
      "id": "et95BD9L-0VT"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "XmJzNF30-0VT"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question 2 – Creating test data\n",
        "\n",
        "The IT department needs some test data before connecting the real sensors.\n",
        "\n",
        "Create:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. A `3 × 4` array containing only zeros.\n",
        "2. A `2 × 5` array containing random values between 0 and 1.\n",
        "3. An array containing the numbers from 10 to 30 using `np.arange()`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Display the three arrays.\n"
