      "source": [
        "### Question 10 – Finding high-temperature equipment\n",
        "\n",
        "The maintenance department considers a reading above **28°C** to be a warning.\n",
        "\n",
        "Using `equipment_temperature`:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Create a Boolean mask for temperatures above 28°C.\n",
        "2. Display the mask.\n",
        "3. Use the mask to display only the warning readings.\n",
        "4. Count how many warning readings are present.\n"
      ],
      "id": "GODZt8TO-0VX"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "PKFJtbeG-0VY",
        "outputId": "b702c7a7-a41b-42b7-a2db-2e9a622a70aa"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[24.5 25.1 23.8 27.4 29.2 26.8 31.5 22.9 28.1 30.4]\n",
            "[False False False False  True False  True False  True  True]\n",
            "[29.2 31.5 28.1 30.4]\n",
            "4\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 10 here\n",
        "boolean_flag=equipment_temperature>28\n",
        "print(equipment_temperature)\n",
        "print(boolean_flag)\n",
        "print(equipment_temperature[boolean_flag])\n",
        "print(np.sum(boolean_flag))"
      ],
      "id": "PKFJtbeG-0VY"
    },
    {
