      "metadata": {
        "id": "FmCUR4nc-0VY"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question 12 – Finding high electricity consumption\n",
        "\n",
        "The university wants to identify all months in which the Academic Block consumed more than **50,000 kWh**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Using NumPy:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Create a condition.\n",
        "2. Use Boolean indexing to get the corresponding energy values.\n",
        "3. Use `np.where()` to find their positions.\n",
        "4. Use those positions with the `months` array to find the month names.\n"
      ],
      "id": "FmCUR4nc-0VY"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "QEFRmy9G-0VY",
        "outputId": "7db6b85a-41d6-48ae-e2c6-dca643b26813"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[[51000 23800 36000]\n",
            " [52500 24600 37100]\n",
            " [51800 24100 36500]\n",
            " [50200 23200 35400]]\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 12 here\n",
        "condition=monthly_energy[:,0]>50000\n",
        "print(monthly_energy[condition])\n",
