    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "vas1THIt-0VZ"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question 15 – Combining two measurements\n",
        "\n",
        "For each month, the operations team wants to use the actual electricity consumption when it is available. If the value is 0, it should use a backup estimate.\n",
        "\n",
        "Create two small NumPy arrays:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "actual = [42000, 0, 44800, 0, 47800]\n",
        "backup = [41000, 43000, 44000, 45500, 47000]\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Use `np.where()` to create a final array that:\n",
        "\n",
        "- uses `backup` when `actual` is 0,\n",
        "- otherwise uses `actual`.\n"
      ],
      "id": "vas1THIt-0VZ"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "dAewJuFT-0VZ",
        "outputId": "e05bf68d-e0a6-4464-ce54-95495f1d6b2d"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[42000     0 44800     0 47800]\n",
            "[41000 43000 44000 45500 47000]\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 15 here\n",
        "actual=np.array([42000,0,44800,0,47800])\n",
        "print(actual)\n",
        "backup=np.array([41000,43000,44000,45500,47000])\n",
        "print(backup)"
      ],
      "id": "dAewJuFT-0VZ"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PHZPO06S-0VZ"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Part E – Concatenating and Deleting Data\n",
        "\n",
        "### Question 16 – Adding a new facility\n",
        "\n",
        "A new **Sports Complex** has been added to the campus.\n",
        "\n",
        "Its monthly electricity consumption is:\n",
        "\n",
        "`[12500, 13000, 12800, 13500, 14200, 15000, 15800, 16200, 15500, 14800, 13700, 12900]`\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Convert the data into a NumPy array.\n",
        "2. Reshape it into a single column.\n",
        "3. Add it to `monthly_energy` using `np.concatenate()` with the correct axis.\n",
        "4. Store the final array as `energy_with_sports`.\n",
        "5. Check its shape.\n"
      ],
      "id": "PHZPO06S-0VZ"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "jP3yDvr8-0VZ",
        "outputId": "6d324719-6bd1-444f-b20f-1ee6f9a6ffef"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[[42000 18500 31000 12500]\n",
            " [43500 19200 31800 13000]\n",
            " [44800 20100 32500 12800]\n",
            " [46200 21500 33100 13500]\n",
            " [47800 22100 34000 14200]\n",
            " [49500 23000 35200 15000]\n",
            " [51000 23800 36000 15800]\n",
            " [52500 24600 37100 16200]\n",
            " [51800 24100 36500 15500]\n",
            " [50200 23200 35400 14800]\n",
            " [47500 21800 33900 13700]\n",
            " [45000 20500 32500 12900]]\n",
            "(12, 4)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 16 here\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "sports_complex = np.array([\n",
        "    12500, 13000, 12800, 13500, 14200, 15000,\n",
        "    15800, 16200, 15500, 14800, 13700, 12900\n",
        "])\n",
        "sports_complex=sports_complex.reshape(12,1)\n",
        "energy_with_sports=np.concatenate((monthly_energy,sports_complex),axis=1)\n",
        "print(energy_with_sports)\n",
        "print(energy_with_sports.shape)\n"
      ],
      "id": "jP3yDvr8-0VZ"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fPMasSkf-0Va"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question 17 – Adding a new month\n",
        "\n",
        "Suppose the university receives data for one additional month:\n",
        "\n",
        "`[46500, 21000, 33000]`\n",
        "\n",
        "Add this as a new row to `monthly_energy` using `np.concatenate()`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Store the result as `energy_extended`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Check its shape before and after concatenation.\n"
      ],
      "id": "fPMasSkf-0Va"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "r_Wop2na-0Va",
        "outputId": "f1dc90db-c679-4944-b009-9462c98967a6"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[[42000 18500 31000]\n",
            " [43500 19200 31800]\n",
            " [44800 20100 32500]\n",
            " [46200 21500 33100]\n",
            " [47800 22100 34000]\n",
            " [49500 23000 35200]\n",
            " [51000 23800 36000]\n",
            " [52500 24600 37100]\n",
            " [51800 24100 36500]\n",
            " [50200 23200 35400]\n",
            " [47500 21800 33900]\n",
            " [45000 20500 32500]\n",
            " [46500 21000 33000]]\n",
            "(13, 3)\n",
            "[[46500 21000 33000]]\n"
