          "text": [
            "[47650.         21866.66666667 34083.33333333]\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 21 here\n",
        "average_facility_energy=np.mean(monthly_energy,axis=0)\n",
        "print(average_facility_energy)"
      ],
      "id": "rfc8y-AT-0Vb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DirHi58f-0Vb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question 22 – Student visits\n",
        "\n",
        "Using `monthly_visits`:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Find the total yearly visits for each facility.\n",
        "2. Find the average monthly visits for each facility.\n",
        "3. Find the month with the highest total campus visits.\n",
        "4. Display that month's name and total number of visits.\n",
        "\n",
        "Use NumPy operations rather than loops.\n"
      ],
      "id": "DirHi58f-0Vb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xgMzAxv0-0Vb",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "16df0c32-3bc9-45df-9366-0a889efe8efe"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[2140 1800 2890]\n",
            "[178.33333333 150.         240.83333333]\n",
            "8\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 22 here\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "monthly_visits = np.array([\n",
        "    [120, 150, 180, 200, 170, 160, 190, 210, 220, 200, 180, 160],\n",
        "    [100, 120, 140, 160, 150, 130, 170, 180, 190, 170, 150, 140],\n",
        "    [200, 220, 210, 230, 250, 240, 260, 270, 280, 260, 240, 230]\n",
        "])\n",
        "yearly_visits =  np.sum(monthly_visits,axis=1)\n",
        "print(yearly_visits)\n",
        "average_monthly = np.mean(monthly_visits,axis=1)\n",
        "print(average_monthly)\n",
        "highest_total = np.sum(monthly_visits,axis=0)\n",
        "c = np.argmax(highest_total)\n",
        "print(c)"
      ],
      "id": "xgMzAxv0-0Vb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jUOuj0C1-0Vb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question 23 – Cumulative electricity consumption\n",
        "\n",
        "The finance department wants a running total of electricity consumption throughout the year.\n",
        "\n",
        "Use `cumsum(axis=0)` on `monthly_energy`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Display:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. The cumulative values for January, February and March.\n",
        "2. The final cumulative value for each facility.\n",
        "\n",
        "Think about why `axis=0` is suitable here.\n"
      ],
      "id": "jUOuj0C1-0Vb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7CSHYpys-0Vc",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "c4f56255-89a2-4a2f-fc1c-d3a721e2b65b"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[[ 100  200  300]\n",
