      "source": [
        "# Part G – Broadcasting\n",
        "\n",
        "### Question 24 – Applying a monthly adjustment\n",
        "\n",
        "During summer, electricity consumption is expected to increase.\n",
        "\n",
        "The estimated monthly adjustment factors are:\n",
        "\n",
        "`[0.95, 0.96, 0.98, 1.00, 1.02, 1.05, 1.08, 1.10, 1.06, 1.02, 0.98, 0.96]`\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Create a NumPy array containing these factors.\n",
        "2. Reshape it so that its shape becomes `(12, 1)`.\n",
        "3. Use broadcasting to multiply it with `monthly_energy`.\n",
        "4. Store the result as `adjusted_energy`.\n",
        "5. Print both shapes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not manually create a 12 × 3 array of factors.\n"
      ],
      "id": "EX8Lak5H-0Vc"
