      "source": [
        "### Question 31 – Save and load NumPy data\n",
        "\n",
        "The university wants to save its cleaned occupancy data for use in another notebook.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Save `weekly_occupancy` as `weekly_occupancy.npy` using `np.save()`.\n",
        "2. Load the file using `np.load()`.\n",
        "3. Store the loaded data as `loaded_occupancy`.\n",
        "4. Display its shape.\n",
        "5. Check whether the loaded array is equal to the original array.\n",
        "\n",
        "This question is about using NumPy's own `.npy` format.\n"
      ],
      "id": "IeneaOrw-0Ve"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1Uebldur-0Ve",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "3f153cc9-2985-49ee-ff73-9584f0cf265e"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Shape: (7, 5)\n",
            "Arrays are equal: True\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 31 here\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1. Save weekly_occupancy\n",
        "np.save(\"weekly_occupancy.npy\", weekly_occupancy)\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Load the file\n",
        "loaded_occupancy = np.load(\"weekly_occupancy.npy\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3. Display shape\n",
        "print(\"Shape:\", loaded_occupancy.shape)\n",
        "\n",
        "# 4. Check whether loaded array equals original array\n",
        "print(\"Arrays are equal:\", np.array_equal(weekly_occupancy, loaded_occupancy))"
      ],
      "id": "1Uebldur-0Ve"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
