        "id": "b3cUhgoo-0Ve"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Final Case Study Questions\n",
        "\n",
        "### Question 32 – Which facility uses the most electricity?\n",
        "\n",
        "Use `monthly_energy` to find the facility with the highest total yearly electricity consumption.\n",
        "\n",
        "Your program should:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Calculate the yearly total for each facility.\n",
        "2. Find the position of the highest value.\n",
        "3. Use that position to find the facility name.\n",
        "4. Display the facility name and its total consumption.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not use a Python loop.\n"
      ],
      "id": "b3cUhgoo-0Ve"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "u6pJmxVk-0Ve",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "f411ea5e-fd89-4503-aaa0-897b6fb50f4c"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Facility: Administrative Block\n",
            "Total yearly electricity consumption: 300\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "facility_names = np.array([\n",
        "    \"Library\",\n",
        "    \"Hostel\",\n",
        "    \"Laboratory\",\n",
        "    \"Canteen\",\n",
        "    \"Academic Block\",\n",
        "    \"Sports Complex\",\n",
        "    \"Auditorium\",\n",
        "    \"Administrative Block\"\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Yearly total for each facility\n",
        "yearly_total = np.sum(monthly_energy, axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Position of highest consumption\n",
        "highest_position = np.argmax(yearly_total)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Facility name\n",
        "facility_name = facility_names[highest_position]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display result\n",
        "print(\"Facility:\", facility_name)\n",
        "print(\"Total yearly electricity consumption:\", yearly_total[highest_position])"
      ],
      "id": "u6pJmxVk-0Ve"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HO58pV12-0Ve"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question 33 – Which month was busiest?\n",
        "\n",
        "Using `monthly_visits`:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Calculate total campus visits for every month.\n",
        "2. Find the index of the month with the highest total visits.\n",
        "3. Display the month name.\n",
        "4. Display the total number of visits.\n",
        "\n",
        "Try to solve the complete question using NumPy.\n"
      ],
      "id": "HO58pV12-0Ve"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TkuQZFaG-0Vf",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "7925cc22-8981-4d14-9a85-eed9513d9696"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Busiest month: September\n",
            "Total visits: 690\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 33 here\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1. Total visits for every month\n",
        "monthly_total = np.sum(monthly_visits, axis=0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Index of month with highest visits\n",
        "highest_position = np.argmax(monthly_total)\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3. Month names\n",
        "month_names = np.array([\n",
        "    \"January\", \"February\", \"March\", \"April\",\n",
        "    \"May\", \"June\", \"July\", \"August\",\n",
        "    \"September\", \"October\", \"November\", \"December\"\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "# 4. Find busiest month\n",
        "busiest_month = month_names[highest_position]\n",
        "\n",
        "# 5. Display result\n",
        "print(\"Busiest month:\", busiest_month)\n",
        "print(\"Total visits:\", monthly_total[highest_position])"
      ],
      "id": "TkuQZFaG-0Vf"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_StERK5j-0Vf"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question 34 – Find classrooms that need attention\n",
        "\n",
        "The university wants to identify classrooms where occupancy was **below 50% at least once** during the week.\n",
        "\n",
        "Using `weekly_occupancy`:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Find the occupancy values below 50%.\n",
        "2. Find the corresponding positions using NumPy.\n",
        "3. Identify which classroom columns are involved.\n",
        "4. Display the result clearly.\n",
        "\n",
        "You may use indexing, Boolean masks and `np.where()`.\n"
      ],
      "id": "_StERK5j-0Vf"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "D1lzWhrV-0Vf",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "c13cfffd-1b8d-4547-d74a-16106396f20a"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Occupancy values below 50%:\n",
            "[49 42 38 45 40 35]\n",
            "\n",
            "Positions:\n",
            "(array([5, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6]), array([4, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4]))\n",
            "\n",
            "Classrooms that need attention:\n",
            "Room 101\n",
            "Room 102\n",
            "Room 103\n",
            "Room 104\n",
            "Room 105\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Write your code for Question 34 here\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# Classroom names\n",
        "classroom_names = np.array([\n",
        "    \"Room 101\",\n",
        "    \"Room 102\",\n",
        "    \"Room 103\",\n",
        "    \"Room 104\",\n",
        "    \"Room 105\",\n",
        "    \"Room 106\",\n",
        "    \"Room 107\",\n",
        "    \"Room 108\"\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1. Find values below 50%\n",
        "mask = weekly_occupancy < 50\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Find positions of those values\n",
        "positions = np.where(mask)\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3. Classroom column positions\n",
        "classroom_positions = positions[1]\n",
        "\n",
        "# 4. Find unique classroom columns\n",
        "classrooms = np.unique(classroom_positions)\n",
        "\n",
        "# 5. Display result\n",
        "print(\"Occupancy values below 50%:\")\n",
        "print(weekly_occupancy[mask])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nPositions:\")\n",
        "print(positions)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nClassrooms that need attention:\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for position in classrooms:\n",
        "    print(classroom_names[position])"
      ],
      "id": "D1lzWhrV-0Vf"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e8jK6yea-0Vf"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Question 35 – Energy efficiency check\n",
        "\n",
        "The university wants to compare electricity consumption with student visits.\n",
        "\n",
        "For each facility:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Calculate total yearly electricity consumption.\n",
        "2. Calculate total yearly student visits.\n",
        "3. Calculate electricity consumption per student visit.\n",
        "4. Display the three resulting values.\n",
        "5. Identify the facility with the highest electricity consumption per visit.\n",
        "\n",
        "Use vectorized NumPy operations.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the final step of the case study: turning raw numerical arrays into a simple decision that can help campus management.\n"
      ],
      "id": "e8jK6yea-0Vf"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "CPtFdl3g-0Vf",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "7107ac83-6a7f-4d22-95fb-12e8b43ca861"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Yearly electricity: [571800 262400 409000]\n",
            "Yearly visits: [111700  73750  82150]\n",
            "Energy per visit: [5.11906893 3.5579661  4.9786975 ]\n",
            "Facility: Academic Block\n",
            "Highest consumption per visit: 5.119068934646374\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# Re-initialize monthly_energy and monthly_visits to their original values\n",
        "monthly_energy = np.array([\n",
        "    [42000, 18500, 31000],\n",
        "    [43500, 19200, 31800],\n",
        "    [44800, 20100, 32500],\n",
        "    [46200, 21500, 33100],\n",
        "    [47800, 22100, 34000],\n",
        "    [49500, 23000, 35200],\n",
        "    [51000, 23800, 36000],\n",
        "    [52500, 24600, 37100],\n",
        "    [51800, 24100, 36500],\n",
        "    [50200, 23200, 35400],\n",
        "    [47500, 21800, 33900],\n",
        "    [45000, 20500, 32500]\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "monthly_visits = np.array([\n",
        "    [8200, 5400, 6100],\n",
        "    [8500, 5600, 6250],\n",
        "    [8700, 5750, 6400],\n",
        "    [9100, 5900, 6650],\n",
        "    [9500, 6200, 6900],\n",
        "    [9800, 6500, 7200],\n",
        "    [10200, 6800, 7500],\n",
        "    [10400, 7000, 7700],\n",
        "    [10100, 6750, 7450],\n",
        "    [9600, 6300, 7000],\n",
        "    [9000, 5900, 6650],\n",
        "    [8600, 5650, 6350]\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "facility_names = np.array([\"Academic Block\", \"Library\", \"Hostel\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Yearly electricity for each facility\n",
        "yearly_energy = np.sum(monthly_energy, axis=0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Yearly visits for each facility\n",
        "yearly_visits = np.sum(monthly_visits, axis=0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Electricity per visit\n",
        "energy_per_visit = yearly_energy / yearly_visits\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display results\n",
        "print(\"Yearly electricity:\", yearly_energy)\n",
        "print(\"Yearly visits:\", yearly_visits)\n",
        "print(\"Energy per visit:\", energy_per_visit)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Highest energy per visit\n",
        "highest_position = np.argmax(energy_per_visit)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Facility:\", facility_names[highest_position])\n",
        "print(\"Highest consumption per visit:\", energy_per_visit[highest_position])"
      ],
